{%- comment -%}
  PG Ultra Buyer Photos (2026-09-25): the "Buyer Reviews" photo strip for the
  R36S Ultra page, registered in templates/product.pg-ultra.json only.

  WHY IT IS ITS OWN FILE. On the R36S Pro and R36H Pro pages the strip lives
  inside the story section (pg-pro2-story, pg-r36h-story). The Ultra's story
  section was cloned from the Pro's on 2026-09-23 with the strip cut out,
  because the Ultra's Judge.me data had been imported for the Flip SP and must
  not have shown. The owner re-imported the Ultra's own reviews on 2026-09-25
  (369 of them, 4.1 average; Judge.me's product_name in the feed now reads
  "Pocket Era R36S Ultra") and asked for the R36S page's review sections back
  on this page. pg-landing's own reviews (the rating line under the title, the
  rotating review card and the review grid with its histogram at the bottom)
  come back by turning hide_reviews off in the template; this file restores
  the strip, built the way the Pro page builds it, without rewriting the 55KB
  story section. Its notes about the strip being "removed" are history now.

  WHAT IT SHOWS. Every photo of every review Judge.me has synced for this
  product (judgeme.review_widget_data: the photo reviews first, then page
  one), one card per photo, each linking to the review grid at the bottom.
  Nothing is invented: the stars, the name and the text are the review's own,
  and the pill over the rail prints the feed's own average and count, then
  follows the page's rating line once pg-rev-link has rendered it. The Pro page
  pins its sharpest photos first with an allow list (hq_keys); this feed is new,
  so it has no such list yet and shows the feed as it comes. It renders
  nothing while the feed holds fewer than three photos.

  WHERE IT SITS. The script seats the strip in the buy column after the Add to
  cart button (a desktop), or after the last bundle tile; on a phone the buy
  column is a flex column and the strip takes order 6, straight after the
  tiles' run and ahead of the accordions, exactly where the Pro page puts it.
  The rail loops: the photo set is printed five times and the script keeps the
  rail on the middle copy (see loopRail in assets/pgx-pg-ultra-shots.js).

  NOTE, as on the Pro page: the photos are served from
  ae-pic-a1.aliexpress-media.com, so these are imported supplier reviews, not
  reviews collected by this store. Raised with the owner before; shown at the
  owner's request.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign jm = product.metafields.judgeme.review_widget_data.value -%}
{%- assign jm_all = '' | split: '' -%}
{%- if jm -%}
  {%- if jm.photo_gallery -%}{%- assign jm_all = jm_all | concat: jm.photo_gallery -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if jm.reviews -%}{%- assign jm_all = jm_all | concat: jm.reviews -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign shots = 0 -%}
{%- capture shots_html -%}
{%- assign seen2 = '|' -%}
{%- for r in jm_all -%}
{%- assign key2 = '|' | append: r.uuid | append: '|' -%}
{%- unless seen2 contains key2 -%}
{%- assign seen2 = seen2 | append: r.uuid | append: '|' -%}
{%- if r.body != blank -%}{%- assign r_text = r.body -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign r_text = r.body_html | strip_html | strip -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign r_stars = r.rating | plus: 0 -%}
{%- for pic in r.pictures_urls -%}
{%- assign pic_url = pic.huge | default: pic.original | default: pic.compact | default: pic.small -%}
{%- if pic_url != blank -%}
{%- assign shots = shots | plus: 1 -%}
<a class="pg-uls-shot" href="#pg-reviews">
  <img src="{{ pic_url }}" alt="Customer photo from {{ r.reviewer_name | default: 'a verified buyer' | escape }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" width="400" height="500">
  <span class="pg-uls-cap">
    <span class="st">{%- for s in (1..5) -%}{%- if s <= r_stars -%}&#9733;{%- else -%}&#9734;{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}</span>
    <span class="nm">{{ r.reviewer_name | default: 'Verified buyer' | escape }}</span>
    {%- if r_text != blank -%}<span class="tx">{{ r_text | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
  </span>
</a>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if shots > 2 -%}
{%- assign uls_avg = jm.average_rating | times: 1.0 | round: 1 -%}
<style>
  /* the strip: the Pro page's rules, renamed. min-width:0 and overflow:hidden
     keep a horizontal scroller from widening the buy column (pg-page-polish
     does the same for the Pro's strip). */
  #pgx .pg-uls-shots{margin:16px 0 4px;min-width:0;max-width:100%;overflow:hidden;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}
  #pgx .pg-uls-shots-h{display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:flex-end;gap:10px;margin:0 2px 9px}
  /* under the headline the caption keeps only its "Swipe" hint, right-aligned;
     the BUYER REVIEWS words read as a second title and are hidden */
  #pgx .pg-uls-shots-h b{display:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#fff}
  #pgx .pg-uls-shots-h span{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#C79BEA;white-space:nowrap}
  /* the "loved by" header over the photo rail: our purple pill with the page's
     own rating and review count, the purple gradient second line. No invented
     customer counts. */
  #pgx .pg-uls-loved{text-align:center;margin:30px 0 6px}
  #pgx .pg-uls-loved-pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#7A2FA2,#9B4BC4 55%,#B478E0);color:#fff;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.02em;line-height:1;box-shadow:0 12px 26px -14px rgba(155,75,196,.9)}
  #pgx .pg-uls-loved-pill .st{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.08em}
  #pgx .pg-uls-loved h3{margin:12px 0 0;font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:27px;line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#fff}
  #pgx .pg-uls-loved h3 span{display:block;background:linear-gradient(100deg,#F3E8FF 0%,#D9B3F5 30%,#B06CE8 60%,#8B3FB8 100%);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent}
  /* the rail loops (the set is printed five times; the script keeps the rail on
     the middle copy). It does not scroll by itself. Cards are a fixed width:
     cqw is 46% of the rail where container units work, 44vw the fallback. */
  #pgx .pg-uls-rail{overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;overscroll-behavior-x:contain;container-type:inline-size;
    scrollbar-width:none;-ms-overflow-style:none;margin:0 -2px;padding:0 2px 4px}
  #pgx .pg-uls-rail::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
  #pgx .pg-uls-track,#pgx .pg-uls-set{display:flex;gap:10px;width:max-content}
  #pgx .pg-uls-shot{flex:0 0 auto;width:min(210px,44vw);width:min(210px,46cqw);display:block;text-decoration:none !important;
    background:#16101F;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;color:#F1EDF7}
  #pgx .pg-uls-shot img{display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/5;object-fit:cover;background:#0D0714}
  #pgx .pg-uls-cap{padding:8px 10px 10px}
  #pgx .pg-uls-cap .st{color:#C79BEA;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;line-height:1}
  #pgx .pg-uls-cap .nm{display:block;margin-top:4px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
  #pgx .pg-uls-cap .tx{margin:3px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.4;color:#CFC4DE;
    display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:3;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
  @media (max-width:900px){
    /* on a phone the buy column is a flex column: the strip follows the tiles'
       run (5) and leads the accordions (6), as on the Pro page */
    #pgx#pgx .pgx-buy > .pg-uls-shots{order:6;margin:6px 0 18px}
  }
</style>
<div id="pg-uls-shots-src" hidden>
  <div class="pg-uls-shots" data-uls="shots">
    <div class="pg-uls-loved"><span class="pg-uls-loved-pill"><span class="st" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span><span data-uls-loved="pill">Rated {{ uls_avg }}/5 &middot; {{ jm.number_of_reviews }} reviews</span></span><h3>Loved by Gamers<span>Just Like You</span></h3></div>
    <div class="pg-uls-shots-h"><b>Buyer Reviews</b><span>Swipe &rarr;</span></div>
    {%- capture shots_clone -%}{{ shots_html | replace: '<a class="pg-uls-shot"', '<a tabindex="-1" class="pg-uls-shot"' }}{%- endcapture -%}
    <div class="pg-uls-rail" data-uls-loop><div class="pg-uls-track"><div class="pg-uls-set">{{ shots_html }}</div><div class="pg-uls-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-uls-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-uls-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div><div class="pg-uls-set" aria-hidden="true">{{ shots_clone }}</div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="{{ 'pgx-pg-ultra-shots.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Ultra Buyer Photos", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG Ultra Buyer Photos"}]}
{% endschema %}
